WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.593 --> 00:00:02.756
(chimes)

00:00:03.727 --> 00:00:05.707
- Informally, we can think of information

00:00:05.707 --> 00:00:08.423
as some message stored or transmitted

00:00:08.423 --> 00:00:10.686
using some medium.

00:00:10.686 --> 00:00:12.804
When you paint, you are
representing your message

00:00:12.804 --> 00:00:15.046
using a continuous pattern with a

00:00:15.046 --> 00:00:18.635
seemingly endless number
of possible forms.

00:00:18.635 --> 00:00:21.777
You are free to express yourself.

00:00:22.477 --> 00:00:24.627
When humans began
developing writing systems,

00:00:24.627 --> 00:00:27.287
we naturally had to divide our world

00:00:27.287 --> 00:00:30.658
into a finite number of atomic units,

00:00:30.658 --> 00:00:33.241
which we expressed using symbols.

00:00:33.241 --> 00:00:34.871
Now any written language

00:00:34.871 --> 00:00:36.786
can be thought of in this way.

00:00:36.786 --> 00:00:39.836
Messages are formed by arranging symbols

00:00:39.836 --> 00:00:42.275
in specific patterns.

00:00:42.275 --> 00:00:44.597
Let's return to 3000 BC

00:00:44.597 --> 00:00:47.728
and explore two ancient writing systems.

00:00:47.728 --> 00:00:51.962
First, in ancient Egypt,
we had hieroglyphics.

00:00:52.101 --> 00:00:54.180
A priestly form of communication

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:56.105
reserved for governmental, fiscal,

00:00:56.105 --> 00:00:59.301
magical and religious purposes.

00:00:59.301 --> 00:01:01.632
It was practiced by a select few writers

00:01:01.632 --> 00:01:04.366
known as scribes, and
writing was generally

00:01:04.366 --> 00:01:07.311
unintelligible to the common people.

00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:09.954
The symbols themselves broadly fall

00:01:09.954 --> 00:01:11.995
into two categories.

00:01:11.995 --> 00:01:14.209
Word signs, which are symbols

00:01:14.209 --> 00:01:17.737
that represent a single
meaningful concept.

00:01:17.737 --> 00:01:20.491
- Back, apple

00:01:20.491 --> 00:01:21.915
- And sound signs.

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:24.306
These symbols represent chunks of sound.

00:01:24.306 --> 00:01:25.935
- Bee
- Zeh

00:01:25.935 --> 00:01:27.437
- Tan
- Kah

00:01:27.437 --> 00:01:30.604
- Now, the total number
of different symbols

00:01:30.604 --> 00:01:34.041
in common use was over 1500,

00:01:34.041 --> 00:01:36.652
and if you divide all of these symbols

00:01:36.652 --> 00:01:39.379
into word signs versus sound signs,

00:01:39.379 --> 00:01:43.445
we find a much smaller
portion of sound signs.

00:01:43.445 --> 00:01:47.693
There were around 140
sound signs, and of these,

00:01:47.693 --> 00:01:52.138
only 33 represented distinct consonants.

00:01:52.138 --> 00:01:56.424
A tiny fraction of all
of the symbols in use.

00:01:56.439 --> 00:01:59.481
At the time, the medium
used to store the symbols

00:01:59.481 --> 00:02:01.154
was primarily rock,

00:02:01.154 --> 00:02:04.258
and this was ideal for
durable inscriptions,

00:02:04.258 --> 00:02:07.361
allowing messages to
travel into the future.

00:02:07.361 --> 00:02:09.802
Mobility was not a main concern

00:02:09.802 --> 00:02:12.325
when communicating messages in this way.

00:02:12.837 --> 00:02:15.361
However, a new physical
medium for storing symbols

00:02:15.361 --> 00:02:17.271
was emerging at the time.

00:02:17.271 --> 00:02:20.896
Along the Nile, silk
deposits left from flooding

00:02:20.896 --> 00:02:24.384
made the surrounding
land extremely fertile

00:02:24.384 --> 00:02:28.489
and one of the many crops
they grew was papyrus.

00:02:28.489 --> 00:02:30.084
It could be sliced into strips

00:02:30.084 --> 00:02:31.919
and these strips were then soaked

00:02:31.919 --> 00:02:34.082
(bell chimes)

00:02:35.574 --> 00:02:38.516
and weaved together, and finally pressed,

00:02:38.516 --> 00:02:41.956
allowing the natural
sugars to act as glue.

00:02:45.156 --> 00:02:46.488
After several days,

00:02:46.488 --> 00:02:50.738
it dried and formed an
almost weightless tablet.

00:02:53.379 --> 00:02:55.639
This medium was ideal for sending messages

00:02:55.639 --> 00:02:58.276
across greater spaces rather than

00:02:58.276 --> 00:03:02.071
the more durable
inscriptions focused on time.

00:03:02.071 --> 00:03:05.185
Now this shift towards
cheap, portable mediums

00:03:05.185 --> 00:03:07.470
for storing symbols coincided

00:03:07.470 --> 00:03:09.605
with the spread of writing into the hands

00:03:09.605 --> 00:03:12.910
of more people for new purposes.

00:03:12.987 --> 00:03:15.983
Gradually, as people began
to write more on papyrus,

00:03:15.983 --> 00:03:19.489
the symbols evolved to
suit more rapid writing.

00:03:19.489 --> 00:03:23.095
This led to a cursive
script known as hieratic.

00:03:23.677 --> 00:03:25.244
For example, here is the world's

00:03:25.244 --> 00:03:28.294
oldest surviving surgical document.

00:03:28.294 --> 00:03:33.294
It's written in hieratic
script, dated to around 1600 BC.

00:03:33.549 --> 00:03:36.095
Now these symbols were
based on hieroglyphics,

00:03:36.095 --> 00:03:38.992
however the pictures
were simplified to match

00:03:38.992 --> 00:03:42.917
the swiftness of writing
in ancient shorthand.

00:03:43.058 --> 00:03:46.533
Also, the number of common symbols in use

00:03:46.533 --> 00:03:50.519
began to shrink down to around 700.

00:03:50.519 --> 00:03:52.787
By escaping from the
heavy medium of stone,

00:03:52.787 --> 00:03:54.487
thought gained lightness.

00:03:54.487 --> 00:03:56.917
A marked increase in writing by hand

00:03:56.917 --> 00:03:58.887
was accompanied by the secularization

00:03:58.887 --> 00:04:01.702
of writing, thought and activity.

00:04:01.702 --> 00:04:04.979
This led to a new writing
system, called demotic,

00:04:04.979 --> 00:04:09.555
around 650 BC, which
was devised specifically

00:04:09.555 --> 00:04:12.439
to facilitate the ease of rapid writing.

00:04:12.823 --> 00:04:16.483
For example, this text is
known as a marriage contract

00:04:16.483 --> 00:04:18.095
and is one of the earliest

00:04:18.095 --> 00:04:20.425
known examples of demotic script.

00:04:20.425 --> 00:04:22.115
It's interesting to notice that there was

00:04:22.115 --> 00:04:23.843
a dramatic reduction again

00:04:23.843 --> 00:04:26.561
in the total number of
symbols with this new system,

00:04:26.561 --> 00:04:31.561
roughly 10% of the total
number of symbols used before.

00:04:32.052 --> 00:04:33.869
This was due to a shift towards the use

00:04:33.869 --> 00:04:36.819
of phonetic symbols, or sound signs

00:04:36.819 --> 00:04:38.457
- Bee
- Zeh

00:04:38.457 --> 00:04:40.032
- Tan
- Kah

00:04:40.032 --> 00:04:43.477
- over word symbols, or meaning signs.

00:04:43.477 --> 00:04:44.738
And the new simplicity meant

00:04:44.738 --> 00:04:48.511
that children could be taught
to write at a young age.

00:04:48.896 --> 00:04:52.218
We see this same pattern
in other cultures.

00:04:52.505 --> 00:04:56.184
Let's return back to 3000
BC and visit Mesopotamia,

00:04:56.184 --> 00:04:58.191
where cuneiform was the writing system

00:04:58.191 --> 00:05:01.186
originally used for fiscal purposes,

00:05:01.186 --> 00:05:03.723
as it was a powerful
method of tracking debt

00:05:03.723 --> 00:05:07.983
and surplus commodities
before the invention of coins.

00:05:08.602 --> 00:05:10.374
For example, here is a document recording

00:05:10.374 --> 00:05:13.182
someone's stock of animal hides,

00:05:13.182 --> 00:05:15.962
and this type of writing
evolved to suit other needs.

00:05:15.962 --> 00:05:17.465
For example, this tablet contains

00:05:17.465 --> 00:05:19.884
a recipe for bread and beer.

00:05:19.884 --> 00:05:23.691
And here's another tablet which
contains a legal document.

00:05:23.691 --> 00:05:25.771
Now originally, the
writing system was used

00:05:25.771 --> 00:05:27.669
by the Sumerians and there were over

00:05:27.669 --> 00:05:31.690
2000 different symbols
in use, which could also

00:05:31.690 --> 00:05:35.718
be divided into word
signs and sound signs.

00:05:36.001 --> 00:05:38.286
Akkadian gradually replaced Sumerian

00:05:38.286 --> 00:05:40.284
as the spoken language,

00:05:40.284 --> 00:05:45.284
and here is the earliest
known dictionary from 2300 BC.

00:05:45.531 --> 00:05:49.938
It contains word lists
in Sumerian and Akkadian,

00:05:49.938 --> 00:05:53.052
and this was discovered in modern Syria.

00:05:53.052 --> 00:05:54.987
When it was adapted by the Akkadians

00:05:54.987 --> 00:05:56.498
and fitted to their language,

00:05:56.498 --> 00:05:59.794
they reduced the number
of symbols to around 600

00:05:59.794 --> 00:06:04.134
and they did this again by
moving towards sound signs.

00:06:04.453 --> 00:06:07.630
Again, we see both
hieroglyphics and cuneiform

00:06:07.630 --> 00:06:10.320
using several hundred sound symbols

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:12.380
in their more evolved forms.

00:06:12.380 --> 00:06:16.214
And as writing systems
escaped their formal usage,

00:06:16.214 --> 00:06:18.492
and spread to more and more people,

00:06:18.492 --> 00:06:20.594
the soil was ripe for the invention

00:06:20.594 --> 00:06:24.873
of a brand new writing
system for the people.

00:06:24.888 --> 00:06:27.717
One of the great discoveries
in the history of writing

00:06:27.717 --> 00:06:30.768
is dated to around 1700 BC.

00:06:30.834 --> 00:06:34.678
The Sinai inscriptions were
found in the Sinai Peninsula.

00:06:34.678 --> 00:06:36.878
and they were about 20 feet apart.

00:06:37.074 --> 00:06:40.436
This was important because
each picture denotes

00:06:40.436 --> 00:06:45.436
a consonant sound and
no word signs are used.

00:06:46.142 --> 00:06:47.735
When sounded out correctly,

00:06:47.735 --> 00:06:51.418
the letters would produce
words in ancient Semitic.

00:06:51.830 --> 00:06:53.738
Although not fully deciphered,

00:06:53.738 --> 00:06:55.609
this message appears to be of the form:

00:06:55.609 --> 00:06:58.613
name, rank and prayer.

00:06:58.613 --> 00:07:02.043
The two words deciphered
are chief and God.

00:07:02.043 --> 00:07:05.633
This innocent example was
part of a writing revolution,

00:07:05.633 --> 00:07:10.106
creating meaning by
merging sound signs only.

00:07:10.106 --> 00:07:15.106
- Back, apple.

00:07:15.144 --> 00:07:19.635
- By 1000 BC, we arrive at
the Phoenician alphabet,

00:07:19.635 --> 00:07:21.739
which emerges along the Mediterranean,

00:07:21.739 --> 00:07:23.103
used by the Phoenicians,

00:07:23.103 --> 00:07:25.639
who were a maritime trading culture.

00:07:26.267 --> 00:07:28.993
The Phoenician writing system
was based on the principle

00:07:28.993 --> 00:07:32.609
that one sign represents one consonant,

00:07:32.609 --> 00:07:35.587
and it was used to write a
northern Semitic language

00:07:35.587 --> 00:07:39.186
containing only 22 symbols total.

00:07:39.186 --> 00:07:41.338
These symbols chosen to
represent these sounds

00:07:41.338 --> 00:07:44.090
were often borrowed for
hieroglyphic pictures

00:07:44.090 --> 00:07:45.505
so that the letter's name

00:07:45.505 --> 00:07:47.513
began with the letter's sound.

00:07:48.370 --> 00:07:51.706
For example, Mem, which stood for water,

00:07:51.706 --> 00:07:55.234
became what we know of as the letter M.

00:07:55.234 --> 00:07:57.311
Aleph, which stood for ox,

00:07:57.311 --> 00:08:00.242
became what we know of as the letter A.

00:08:00.242 --> 00:08:02.483
But the secret power of this alphabet,

00:08:02.483 --> 00:08:04.762
unknown to its inventors, was that

00:08:04.762 --> 00:08:09.549
it did not need Semitic speech
in order to work. - B, C, D

00:08:09.549 --> 00:08:12.797
- Ah, aye, ih, ooh, uh

00:08:12.797 --> 00:08:15.343
- With modest adjustments,
these miraculous letters

00:08:15.343 --> 00:08:17.017
would be fitted to diverse tongues

00:08:17.017 --> 00:08:20.094
of Europe, India and Southeast Asia,

00:08:20.094 --> 00:08:22.324
carrying literacy around the globe.

00:08:22.324 --> 00:08:24.680
- Ma, da.

00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:26.371
- This was the source of the Greek,

00:08:26.371 --> 00:08:30.090
and later Roman, alphabet
forms we know today.

00:08:31.059 --> 00:08:33.956
The idea of an alphabet
is a powerful method

00:08:33.956 --> 00:08:37.390
for transmitting and storing information.

00:08:37.881 --> 00:08:40.550
Realize it doesn't really
matter what the symbols are

00:08:40.550 --> 00:08:41.946
or how you choose them,

00:08:41.946 --> 00:08:43.846
or even what language it's in.

00:08:43.846 --> 00:08:46.745
Information is just a selection

00:08:46.745 --> 00:08:49.806
from a collection of possible symbols.

00:08:51.530 --> 00:08:54.816
And over time, we've
always looked for faster,

00:08:54.816 --> 00:08:57.407
more efficient ways of
transporting information

00:08:57.407 --> 00:09:00.340
across greater and greater spaces.

00:09:00.340 --> 00:09:02.876
And when we try doing
this using new mediums,

00:09:02.876 --> 00:09:06.260
which travel faster than
any human or animal,

00:09:06.260 --> 00:09:09.130
an engineering problem presents itself.

00:09:11.176 --> 00:09:14.200
- Hello? Hello?

00:09:14.200 --> 00:09:16.578
(buzzing)

